N4       IS d = 3 DISTINGUISHED AT ALL?
         fields whose ONLY ramified prime is 3: [(3, -3)]
         the five smallest |D|: [(3, 3), (4, 1), (7, 7), (8, 2), (11, 11)]
         smallest |D| overall: |D| = 3 at d = 3
N4 PASS  d = 3 IS distinguished, and in exactly one way: it is the
         UNIQUE imaginary quadratic field ramified ONLY at 3, and it attains the
         SMALLEST |D| of any imaginary quadratic field.
         AND THE SEAL REQUIRED THIS SENTENCE: those are the same fact.  |D| = 3 is
         minimal BECAUSE 3 is the only ramified prime and 3 is the smallest odd
         prime.  SO THE DISTINCTION IS MINIMALITY -- WHICH IS AXIOM A6 RESTATED,
         NOT AN INDEPENDENT SELECTOR.  The arithmetic did not pick d = 3; the
         minimality axiom did, and the arithmetic followed.

